 so i  would say it's a pretty good reference  point yeah  um now in real life obviously you ba you  write based on your own experiences but  are you typically the one to let the  good ones go like are your friends like  charlie what are you doing  um  i think there's been there's definitely  been times where i have for sure um i'm  kind of like i would say i fall  somewhere in the middle i i feel like  sometimes i am kind of reckless and then  other times  at the opposite so but i've definitely  been guilty of that for sure  what would somebody have to have for  charlie not to let them go  oh good question um great taste in  champagne  um  high tolerance for partying  and they have to be able to make me  laugh  laughter is very important listen  talking about uh letting things go you  are an incredible songwriter and you've  written songs like same old love i don't  care just to name a few there's hundreds  out there do you have a hard time  sometimes letting those songs go to  other artists or is that just part of  being a songwriter being able to just  say okay it's yours now yeah yeah it's  kind of part of it and also it's really  fun to see  other artists sing  your songs that you've written or been a  part of writing with them you know it's  really fun to see how it kind of like  takes on a life on it of its own which  you know maybe it wouldn't have had  if i was singing it so um  it's always really good like it's always  cool to see artists put their own spin  on things that we've written together  especially when they're doing like  videos and performances like it's is  exciting  yeah for sure the video and visuals are  so important to charlie xcx as a fan  like i love always seeing a video like  this it is epic like totally epic a lot  of love went into this video um you're  dancing on your own grave in this video  which yeah you know if i was doing that  somebody in my family would be like what  are you doing you can't do this like is  there somebody in y